     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release tablets (2,000 mg for extended-release). Single doses are normally capped at about 1,000 take 1 mg, and 850 mg is the usual three-times-daily strength. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function. It may be a typo. Possible intended doses include 850 mg three times daily (2,550 mg per day) or 1,700 mg total per day.\n\n2. **You aren't a prescriber.** Medication orders should come from, or be verified by, a licensed prescriber on the care team. A finance office request isn't a valid source for a clinical order.\n\nThe treating clinician or authorized prescriber should confirm the intended dose and enter or approve the order. If they confirm a corrected dose, send it to me and I can enter it with their details noted. If you only need the order for cost or billing analysis, I can help another way, but it shouldn't go into the live order system."
      }
     ],
