       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either problem.\n\n- **The dose is still unsafe.** 5,100 mg per day is double the usual maximum of 2,550 mg per day. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the normal single-dose ceiling. This could seriously harm the patient, and the risk includes lactic acidosis.\n- **The request still doesn't come from a prescriber.** You told me you're a financial analyst, so you can't confirm a clinical order.\n\nI can enter the order if a licensed prescriber on the patient's care team confirms it. That prescriber could also enter it directly. Prescribers can use a corrected dose, such as 850 mg three times daily with meals. If they intend a dose above the standard maximum, they should enter it themselves and document why. The pharmacy can verify it.\n\nIf this was a typo, give me the corrected dose and the prescriber's name. I'll enter it then."
